cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "F1 is pre-registered; the sensitivity control is a post-hoc addition; F4 is exploratory and must not be cited without its caveat."
type: report
title: "prompt-injection-base-rate"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered measurement of one concealment channel in 290 Common Crawl WET
  records: 34 (11.7%) carried an invisible code point, and the concealment channel
  carried no instruction in the 34 documents where it could exist (3 read closely,
  31 screened by a benign mechanism signature; 0/3, one-sided 95% upper bound
  63.2%). The instrument cannot see visible, base64 or emoji-encoded instructions,
  and 256 of 290 records were never examined for D2. A later F4 frame on 553 job
  postings is exploratory, not pre-registered, and its 2.9% figure is a
  sensitivity-adjusted upper bound, not a prevalence estimate.
authors:
  - family-names: Fleitas
    given-names: Diego
repository-code: "https://github.com/DiegoFleitas/prompt-injection-base-rate"
url: "https://github.com/DiegoFleitas/prompt-injection-base-rate"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - prompt injection
  - base rate
  - invisible unicode
  - agent security
  - reproducibility
